## Quality Rules

Before writing, verify every item:

- [ ] Every command in the Commands table is copy-pasteable and correct
- [ ] Architecture bullets describe implications, not just facts
- [ ] Conventions tell the agent what TO DO and what NOT TO DO
- [ ] Guardrails use **NEVER** and give a reason
- [ ] Key Files lists only the 5–8 most important files, not every file
- [ ] No section is vague ("follows best practices" → delete it)
- [ ] Empty sections are omitted entirely
- [ ] Task Context and Definition of Done contain concrete project-specific guidance, not generic promises

**Length is a guideline, not a validation gate.** Aim for a concise guide of
roughly 1–2 pages; completeness and accuracy matter more than a numeric budget.
Do not count characters or tokens, run length-check commands, or repeatedly
rewrite the file to meet a size target. Omit redundant facts while drafting,
then write once. Correct factual errors or failed writes as needed, but stop
when the useful, verified project guidance is saved. Never drop safety-critical
instructions or exact commands just to shorten the file.

